cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Syxplain, please cite it as below."
title: "Syxplain: an AI-scientist agent for interpretable equation discovery"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "HUN-REN AI1Science"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-25"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24528561
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HUN-REN-AI1Science/syxplain"
url: "https://syxplain.ai1science.net"
abstract: >-
  Syxplain finds interpretable equations in tabular and time-series data. An LLM agent
  steers PySR and SINDy searches while exploring blind to known laws. Numerical code
  fits every candidate and chooses the recommended equation coherence first: equations
  that conflict with the scientific context of the data or with statements of the
  literature are excluded, and the rest are ranked by cross-validated error. The
  recommendation is scored once on a holdout and checked against the noise ceiling,
  SHAP effects and known laws.
keywords:
  - symbolic regression
  - equation discovery
  - scientific discovery
  - large language models
  - PySR
  - explainable AI
